## 3. `include/strata/artifact/dequant.hpp` — Scalar Dequantizers

**Responsibilities:** Provides scalar reference dequantizers for Q2_0, Q8_0, Q4_0, Q5_0, IQ4_NL, Q6_K, Q4_K, Q5_K, Q3_K, IQ4_XS, F32, F16, BF16. Used as the validated reference for GPU kernel parity tests.

**Proposed change:** Add a `dequantize_q2_K` implementation (256 elements, 84-byte block) to complete the K-quant family, since the Unsloth UD-Q4_K_XL path references Q2_K in some layers.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/dequant.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/dequant.hpp
@@ -195,6 +195,42 @@
     }
 }

+// ---- Q2_K: 256 elements from an 84-byte super-block. Layout: scales[16] (4-bit high),
+// qs[128] (4-bit low), qh[32] (2-bit high), fp16 d LAST. Transcribed from dequantize_row_q2_K
+// (ggml-quants.c at 3cf03257).
+inline void dequantize_q2_K(const uint8_t* block, float* out) {
+    const uint8_t* scales = block;       // 16
+    const uint8_t* qh = block + 16;      // 32
+    const uint8_t* qs = block + 48;      // 128
+    const float d = fp16_to_fp32(read_u16(block + 82));
+    float* y = out;
+    for (int n = 0; n < 256; n += 64) {
+        const int is = n / 16;
+        const int sc = (scales[is + 0] & 0xF) | ((scales[is + 0] >> 4) << 4);
+        const int m  = (scales[is + 0] >> 4) & 0xF;
+        const float dl = d * (float)sc;
+        const float ml = d * (float)m;
+        for (int l = 0; l < 32; ++l) {
+            const int q1 = (qs[l] & 0x03) | ((qh[l] & 0x03) << 2);
+            const int q2 = (qs[l] >> 2) & 0x03 | ((qh[l] >> 2) & 0x03) << 2;
+            const int q3 = (qs[l] >> 4) & 0x03 | ((qh[l] >> 4) & 0x03) << 2;
+            const int q4 = (qs[l] >> 6) & 0x03 | ((qh[l] >> 6) & 0x03) << 2;
+            y[l + 0]  = dl * (float)q1 - ml;
+            y[l + 32] = dl * (float)q2 - ml;
+            y[l + 64] = dl * (float)q3 - ml;
+            y[l + 96] = dl * (float)q4 - ml;
+        }
+        y += 128;
+        qs += 64;
+        qh += 32;
+    }
+}
+
 // ---- element types
 inline void dequantize_f32(const uint8_t* p, float* out, int n) {
     std::memcpy(out, p, (size_t)n * 4);
```

**Verification cases:**
1. Generate a synthetic Q2_K block with known scale/min and code values; dequantize with `dequantize_q2_K` and compare against a hand-computed expected output for all 256 elements.
2. Dequantize a real Q2_K tensor from a GGUF file and verify every output value lies within `[−min, max]` derived from the block's own scale and min fields.

