## 4. `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — Split Model Shard Resolution

**Responsibilities:** Resolves the shard paths of a split GGUF model from any shard's filename, validates that all shards exist, and returns them in split order.

**Proposed change:** Add a `gguf_split_count()` helper that returns the number of shards without opening files, and a `gguf_split_is_split()` predicate, so callers can decide whether to use `GgufModel` or `GgufFile` without exception handling.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ -18,6 +18,28 @@
 namespace strata {

+/// Whether `path` matches the split-GGUF naming pattern (`-NNNNN-of-MMMMM.gguf`).
+inline bool gguf_split_is_split(const std::string& path) {
+    static const char tag[] = "-of-";
+    const size_t at = path.rfind(tag);
+    if (at == std::string::npos || at < 6 || path[at - 6] != '-' ||
+        path.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5 || path.compare(at + 9, 5, ".gguf") != 0)
+        return false;
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
+        const char a = path[at - 5 + i], b = path[at + 4 + i];
+        if (a < '0' || a > '9' || b < '0' || b > '9') return false;
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
+/// The number of shards a split model has (1 for a non-split path). Does not check file existence.
+inline int gguf_split_count(const std::string& path) {
+    static const char tag[] = "-of-";
+    const size_t at = path.rfind(tag);
+    if (at == std::string::npos || at < 6 || path[at - 6] != '-' ||
+        path.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5 || path.compare(at + 9, 5, ".gguf") != 0)
+        return 1;
+    int n = 0;
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
+        const char b = path[at + 4 + i];
+        if (b < '0' || b > '9') return 1;
+        n = n * 10 + (b - '0');
+    }
+    return n < 1 ? 1 : n;
+}
+
 // Split models: `<name>-00001-of-0000N.gguf` ... `<name>-0000N-of-0000N.gguf`, as llama.cpp's gguf-split names
 // them.  Given ANY shard's path, the shards in split order (the metadata shard, 00001, first); a file without that
 // suffix is a model of one shard.  Only the five digits of the shard number are rewritten, so the directory and
```

**Verification cases:**
1. Call `gguf_split_is_split("model-00001-of-00004.gguf")` → `true`; `gguf_split_is_split("model.gguf")` → `false`; `gguf_split_count("model-00001-of-00004.gguf")` → `4`.
2. Call `gguf_split_paths` on a path where shard 3 is missing; confirm it throws with the missing shard's name in the message, and that `gguf_split_count` still returns 4 (no file check).

