## 5. `include/strata/core/conversation_buffer.hpp` — Snapshot-Owned Host Storage

**Responsibilities:** Provides a segmented byte buffer (`ConversationBuffer`) that never relocates existing payloads on append, supports `visit()` for zero-copy transfer, geometric segment growth, and equality comparison.

**Proposed change:** Add a `shrink_to_fit()` method that releases excess segment capacity after a resize-down, and a `capacity()` accessor reporting total allocated bytes across all segments.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/core/conversation_buffer.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/core/conversation_buffer.hpp
@@ -55,6 +55,18 @@
     size_t bytes() const {
         size_t n = segments_.capacity() * sizeof(Segment);
         for (const auto& segment : segments_) n += segment.capacity();
         return n;
     }
+
+    /// Total allocated bytes across all segments (may exceed size()).
+    size_t capacity() const {
+        size_t n = 0;
+        for (const auto& seg : segments_) n += seg.capacity();
+        return n;
+    }
+
+    /// Release excess capacity in the last segment after a resize-down.
+    void shrink_to_fit() {
+        if (!segments_.empty()) segments_.back().shrink_to_fit();
+    }
+
